<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Miguel Gómez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1858–1921</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Miguel Gómez was a Cuban general of the War of Independence and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a> who served as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> from 1909 to 1913. His election ended the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/occupation-of-japan">American occupation</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-magoon">Charles Magoon</a>. His government was marked by corruption and by the bloody suppression of the Afro-Cuban uprising of 1912.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-miguel-gomez.jpg" alt="José Miguel Gómez" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brown Bros., NY · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Jos%C3%A9_Miguel_G%C3%B3mez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
